# ==============================================================================
# CURSOR & WINDSURF RULES: AUTONOMOUS JOB FINDER, TAILORER & APPLIER PLATFORM
# ==============================================================================

# 1. PROJECT OVERVIEW & ARCHITECTURE
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This workspace hosts an autonomous, multi-tier AI job hunting and application platform.
# It continuously discovers software/AI jobs, evaluates stack match (JEV), tailors
# crisp 1-page XeTeX/LaTeX resumes via Claude Sonnet 3.5, and stages or auto-applies
# on Ashby, Greenhouse, Lever, and custom enterprise portals using ego-browser.
#
# Primary Entrypoints:
# - Master CLI: cli.py
# - MCP Server: engine/mcp/agy_terminal_mcp.py (13 JSON-RPC tools)
# - Database: data/jobs.db (SQLite with WAL mode)
# - Daemon: launchd service com.adarsh.ai_auto_applier (PID tracked in launchctl)
# ==============================================================================

# 2. NON-NEGOTIABLE OPERATIONAL SAFETY RULES
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. ZERO CREDENTIAL HARDCODING:
#    - All candidate information (names, emails, phone numbers, locations, CTC, links)
#      MUST load dynamically from .env via engine.config.
#    - NEVER hardcode personal credentials or private tokens into code, templates, or commits.
#    - .env is strictly gitignored and must never be tracked.
#
# 2. ZERO-PLACEHOLDER SAFETY CIRCUIT BREAKER:
#    - Before staging or applying, engine.config.assert_real_candidate_profile() runs.
#    - If placeholder values (e.g. "Candidate Name", "candidate@example.com") are detected,
#      execution aborts immediately. Applications are NEVER submitted with dummy data.
#
# 3. STRICT 1-PAGE XETEX COMPILATION RULE:
#    - Every tailored resume must compile strictly to EXACTLY 1 page.
#    - Verified programmatically via macOS PDFKit (engine.claude_tailor.get_pdf_page_count).
#    - ZERO whitespace gaps at the bottom; ZERO spillover onto page 2.
#
# 4. TWO-TIER SUBMISSION POLICY:
#    - Remote Contract roles (Himalayas, Mercor, Turing, Alignerr): AUTO_SUBMIT.
#    - Full-Time India roles (Tier-1 Tech, Enterprises): STAGE_AND_VALIDATE.
#      Fill 100% of fields in ego-browser, attach the tailored PDF, and leave the
#      final submit button enabled for user 1-click review.
#
# 5. NO ANTI-BOT OR CAPTCHA BYPASSING:
#    - Never attempt to defeat, bypass, or click through CAPTCHAs, Cloudflare Turnstile,
#      or proof-of-work gates. Leave staged in ego-browser for user manual completion.
# ==============================================================================

# 3. EGO-BROWSER PROFILE JARGON MATRIX
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ego-browser isolates browsing profiles to eliminate authentication popups:
#
# | Profile | Name / Jargon | Purpose & Bound Portals |
# |---|---|---|
# | Profile 1 | "Main Account" / "Personal" | ChatGPT (chatgpt.com), Mercor, Ashby, Microsoft, Stripe, Personal Gmail |
# | Profile 2 | "College Profile" | LinkedIn (jobs & InMail), College Gmail, Overleaf (pdfLaTeX), Academic/Research portals |
# | Default   | "Daily Workload" | High-volume ATS scrapers (Greenhouse, Lever), non-authenticated career boards |
#
# CLI Commands:
# - python3 cli.py switch-account --service <chatgpt|mercor|linkedin|personal_gmail|college_gmail>
# - python3 cli.py check-emails --profile <personal|college> --limit 5
# ==============================================================================

# 4. MODEL CONTEXT PROTOCOL (MCP) RULES
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The MCP server is in engine/mcp/agy_terminal_mcp.py and speaks JSON-RPC 2.0.
#
# Framing Protocol:
# - Dual-mode framing: handles both standard HTTP/LSP Content-Length headers and NDJSON.
# - sys.stdout is STRICTLY RESERVED for JSON-RPC messages.
# - All diagnostic logging, warnings, and error traces MUST write to sys.stderr.
#
# Available MCP Tools:
# 1.  list_jobs(status, priority, limit)
# 2.  get_job_details(job_id)
# 3.  spawn_agy_worker(task_prompt, working_dir, conversation_id, effort, timeout_sec)
# 4.  consult_chatgpt(prompt, timeout_sec)
# 5.  generate_application_pitch(company, title, jd)
# 6.  apply_to_job(url, company, submit, resume_path)
# 7.  tailor_resume_claude(job_id, company, title)
# 8.  switch_browser_account(service, url)
# 9.  check_inbox_emails(profile, limit)
# 10. record_apply_procedure(company, domain, ats_platform, submission_policy, notes)
# 11. track_agent_dispatch(company, conversation_id, agent_type, job_id, role_title, status, notes)
# 12. get_company_dispatches(company)
# 13. get_daemon_status()
# ==============================================================================

# 5. MULTI-AGENT DELEGATION PATTERN
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# When acting as an autonomous agent in this repository:
#
# Step 1 (Research & Triage):
# - Query jobs using list_jobs(status="EVALUATED", priority="CRITICAL_PRIORITY").
# - Check prior threads for target company via get_company_dispatches(company).
#
# Step 2 (Resume Strategy):
# - If Tier-1 FTE role or high-suitability remote role: invoke tailor_resume_claude.
# - Otherwise: use select_specialization_resume() to compile the dedicated archetype.
#
# Step 3 (Application & Staging):
# - Delegate or run apply_to_job(url=..., company=..., submit=False).
# - Validate that form fields and file attachment succeeded in ego-browser.
#
# Step 4 (Dispatch Memory):
# - Record the outcome using track_agent_dispatch() so subsequent roles can resume
#   the existing company conversation.
# ==============================================================================

# 6. MASTER RESUMES & ARCHETYPES
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Four specialization archetypes are maintained in master_resumes/:
# 1. RESUME_1_AI_ENGINEER.tex         -> AI / GenAI / LLM / Agent Systems
# 2. RESUME_2_DATA_ENGINEER.tex       -> Data Platform / Spark / Glue / Kafka Lakehouse
# 3. RESUME_3_SWE_BACKEND.tex         -> Backend / Distributed Systems / Go / FastAPI
# 4. RESUME_4_GENERAL_ENGINEERING.tex  -> General SWE / Algorithms / Full-Stack
#
# Compile offline using Tectonic:
# - python3 cli.py compile-latex --tex <path_to_tex>
# ==============================================================================
